//! check: run(exit=1, stdout="error: parse")
//! phase: run
//! conforms: std.x.json, err.row, err.propagate
//!
//! `root`'s one row, ridden out of `main` so the RECORD names it: a
//! document that is not RFC 8259 is `parse` at the DOM half's door,
//! before any handle exists. One tag, one file — the sc07 shape, because
//! `error: parse` on the record is the toolchain's word where a handler
//! printing "it was parse" would be this repository's.
//!
//! `root` has no `missing`: the root of a valid document always exists,
//! and a tag no argument can reach stays off the signature (§14's sc12
//! rule).
//!
//! Two lanes at this sprint's pin; lupin flips on a pin, not an edit
//! (see dom_navigation.lu).

use std.x.json

fn main() -> !int {
    json.root("{{")?
    0
}
